{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552202-atlanta-by-night","id":1552202,"title":"Atlanta by Night","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-08T10:32:24-07:00","id":1552202,"title":"Atlanta by Night","content":"So, I am starting my own Atlanta by Night (Set in 2010-2020) I know the Sabbat up and leave sometime in 2008 and creates a vacuum. I read somewhere that Victoria Ash returns and claims praxis in the name of the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> Does anyone know or can provide anything else?<br /> <br /> What I have so far. Victoria Ash- Claims the city in the name of Camarilla in 2009 (New Years) she is supported by a mix of other kindred who see a chance to gain recognition and power. Several Anarchs have come to the city during the seize in power and (2-3 Anarch leaders have come to power, causing problems for the new established city of the Ivory tower) At some point going to have the Lasombra join and have a chance at power here, as I know some point after 2010, they join the Ivory Tower. <br /> I have Aunt Bedelia coming back to the city (as she escaped the Sabbat invasion) but not sure what role she will play. Also Salvatore Giovanni is known to be here, as an Independent will or would he support the new regime or work against it? <br /> <br /> I have made up a few Kindred and inserted them in parts of my works. Stil at this point working on several details, not my first by night run, but the first as a true restart for a Sect and how it would look changing power created by a city being abandoned. <br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-08T13:21:07-07:00","id":1552213,"title":"","content":"You always could dust off the Blood Curse<br /> That mysterious plague plunged numerous Cainites into madness before destroying them between &quot;97 and &quot;99. The disease hit Atlanta <i>hard</i><br /> A decade is nothing in the Vampire world and no one really knows what caused the Blood plague; it is widely believed it was a virus artificially bred by the Sabbat and actually no one really knows how Owain ap Ieuan, a 5th Generation Ventrue antitribu cured it (who in the blood curse trilogy was an advisor of Prince Benison and worth to mention he drained Joseph of Arimathea, the guardian of the Grail. He obtained the power of healing ever since he drank the blood of Joseph but he never touched the Holy Grail and even forgot everything about it... but the knowledge might still be in his mind just locked away.)<br /> It could return any time to ravage the city - it even could have ties with Metathiax, the powerful demon bound to the region of Montr\u00e9al, sealed there by Native Americans, one of the 36 demons of the Decani \u2013 creatures who barter in disease. Maybe the infernalists of Montr\u00e9al &quot;smuggled&quot; the Demon's influence to Atlanta. While not really a neigboring city, Metathiax especially hate Native Americans and enjoys sacrificing Native Americans the most. The Shadowlands of Atlanta are shrouded in perpetual fire. Barrow-Flames spill from the Tempest near forgotten indian grave mounds as the spectres of long dead tribes want vengeance. Metathiax could sent his minions to Atlanta to torture these already vengeful spectres and their mortal descendants or establish even a new Blood Circle there. Blood spilled in the circle instantly becomes diseased. Infernalists drink this vitae in worship of their master. They thereby imbue their bodies with virulent plagues which they pass on to mortals and Cainites alike. This would be in tune with the mysterious Blood Curse origin or re-appearance<br /> <br /> <br /> In Night of Prophecy the Sabbat struggled to overtake the infrastructure of the city, and clashed with the Giovanni that have remained in the city and depending how V5 you play, the Sabbat went to the Gehenna War (and the Second Inquisition's Operation under FIRSTLIGHT cleared out the rest of the Sabbat) and the Camarilla severly weakened and never fully recovered the Giovanni easly could grab the city... and nowdays since the Family Gathering Atlanta could be a stronghold of the Hecata - it would make an especially interesting situation with Bedelia if you take the V20 story in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. She was portryed as a necromancer and it was a possibility she\u2019ll raise up an army of the Restless Dead and go to war against the Atlanta Sabbat. If the Sabbat was evicted and/or the Hecata took root, she and her Wraiths could easly shake things up. And of course New Orleans is not that far, and Alexander Silverson wanted to find and wake his Sire, because he belived Aunt Bedelia could help the Camarilla, clear out the relegiously devout followers of Vodou (Samedi maybhaps - another possible tie to the Hecata-Bedelia/Atlanta enmity) and her to become Prince of New Orleans <br /> <br /> If you are fan of crossovers, Atlanta had a major Pentex office and the Glasswalkers and the Bone Gnawlers were especially common - and both tribes had quiet cordial working relationship with Cainites, the Glasswalkers and the Venture and the Bone Gnawlers and the Nosferatu share area of interests and quietly worked out small truces<br /> <br /> And one of the stops of the Midnight Express is within Atlanta's Necropolis just for the fun with Bedelia's wraiths<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.