t even could have ties with Metathiax, the powerful demon bound to the region of Montr\u00e9al, sealed there by Native Americans, one of the 36 demons of the Decani \u2013 creatures who barter in disease. Maybe the infernalists of Montr\u00e9al &quot;smuggled&quot; the Demon's influence to Atlanta. While not really a neigboring city, Metathiax especially hate Native Americans and enjoys sacrificing Native Americans the most. The Shadowlands of Atlanta are shrouded in perpetual fire. Barrow-Flames spill from the Tempest near forgotten indian grave mounds as the spectres of long dead tribes want vengeance. Metathiax could sent his minions to Atlanta to torture these already vengeful spectres and their mortal descendants or establish even a new Blood Circle there. Blood spilled in the circle instantly becomes diseased. Infernalists drink this vitae in worship of their master. They thereby imbue their bodies with virulent plagues which they pass on to mortals and Cainites alike. This would be in tune with the mysterious Blood Curse origin or re-appearance<br /> <br /> <br /> In Night of Prophecy the Sabbat struggled to overtake the infrastructure of the city, and clashed with the Giovanni that have remained in the city and depending how V5 you play, the Sabbat went to the Gehenna War (and the Second Inquisition's Operation under FIRSTLIGHT cleared out the rest of the Sabbat) and the Camarilla severly weakened and never fully recovered the Giovanni easly could grab the city... and nowdays since the Family Gathering Atlanta could be a stronghold of the Hecata - it would make an especially interesting situation with Bedelia if you take the V20 story in Beckett's Jyhad Diary. She was portryed as a necromancer and it was a possibility she\u2019ll raise up an army of the Restless Dead and go to war against the Atlanta Sabbat. If the Sabbat was evicted and/or the Hecata took root, she and her Wraiths could easly shake things up. And of course New Orleans is not that far, and A